    ],
    [
      "P003",
      "8 Electrical Systems\nSection",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P004",
      "4 Shipboard Installation and Tests\n4-8-4\n27\nElectrical Equipment in Hazardous Areas",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P005",
      "27.1 General (2020)",
      false,
      "heading",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P006",
      "Hazardous areas are spaces where flammable or explosive gases, vapors or dust are normally present, or\nlikely to be present.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P007",
      "Hazardous areas are to be classified based on the likelihood of presence and the\nconcentration and type of flammable atmosphere, as well as in terms of the extent of the space.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P008",
      "Electrical\nequipment is not to be installed in hazardous areas unless it is essential for safety or for operational\npurposes.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P009",
      "Where the installation of electrical equipment in such location is necessary, it is to be selected\nbased on its suitability for the hazardous area so classified.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P010",
      "Such equipment is to be as specified in the\nappropriate sections of the Rules, as indicated below.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P011",
      "Generally electrical equipment certified for use in hazardous areas in accordance with the IEC 60079 series\nis considered suitable for use in temperatures from –20°C to 40°C (–4°F to 104°F).",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P012",
      "Account is to be taken\nof the temperature at the point of installation when selecting electrical equipment for installation in\nhazardous areas.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P013",
      "Fans used for the ventilation of the hazardous areas are to be of non-sparking construction in accordance\nwith 4-8-3/11.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P014",
      "Note: The standard atmospheric conditions defined in IEC Publication 60079-0 relate to the explosion characteristics of\nthe atmosphere and not the operating range of the equipment.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P015",
      "27.3 Hazardous Areas",
      false,
      "heading",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P016",
      "27.3.1 General",
      false,
      "heading",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S002"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P017",
      "The following spaces are, in general, to be regarded as hazardous areas:\ni)\nTanks containing flammable liquids having a flash point of 60°C (140°F) or below.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P018",
      "ii)\nHolds containing solid bulk cargoes liable to release flammable gases or dust.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P019",
      "iii)\nHolds or enclosed cargo spaces containing cargoes that are likely to emit flammable gases\nor vapors (e.g. dangerous goods, vehicles with fuel in their tanks, etc.)\niv)\nAn enclosed or semi-enclosed space:\n● Having a direct access or opening into the hazardous areas defined in i), ii) or iii),\nthrough a door, a ventilation opening, etc.;\n● Immediately adjacent to the hazardous areas defined in i); or\n● Containing pumps or piping used for conveying liquid described in i).",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P020",
      "v)\nA defined zone in open space:\n● 3 m (10 ft) from an opening to the hazardous areas defined in i), ii), iii) or iv), such as\na door, a ventilation opening, a tank vent, etc., unless as otherwise indicated in\n4-8-4/27.3.2 and 4-8-4/27.3.3;\n● Immediately adjacent to the hazardous area defined in i); or\n● In way of pumps or piping used for conveying liquid described in i).",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P021",
      "27.3.2 Specific Vessel Types",
      false,
      "heading",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P022",
      "Due to the nature of the cargoes carried, or the types of operation performed at sea, hazardous\nareas are defined for the following vessel types in the appropriate sections of the Rules:\ni)\nOil carriers carrying crude oil or refined oil products having a flash point of 60°C (140°F)\nor below.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P023",
      "See 5C-1-7/31.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P024",
      "ii)\nBulk carriers carrying coal or other dangerous cargoes in bulk.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P025",
      "See 5C-3-7/3.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P026",
      "RULES FOR BUILDING AND CLASSING MARINE VESSELS • 2021",
      false,
      "heading",
      "836:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
